  "body": "The _by far primary_ use case of this API is binary data. However, if it's easy and causes _no_ performance or implementation concerns, it'd be cool for them to be generic in what they take in.\n\nThe constraints so far that I can see are:\n- We currently concatenate buffers (#4); if we want genericness but still want concatenation, we need to duck-type on `concat` methods.\n- Our watermarks are currently byte-based; if we want genericness, we need to duck-type on `length` properties (perhaps defaulting to length 1?)\n\nI do _not_ intend to prioritize work on genericizing these streams, but if we can keep the possibility in the back of our minds while designing the API, we might end up with something genericizable, in which case we can then add this after all the binary data semantics are nailed down 100%.\n",
